{
  "summary": "The Clean Architecture blueprint for the ecommerce_platform specifies strict unidirectional dependencies flowing inward toward the Domain layer. Six critical violations were discovered: the Application layer imports Presentation and Infrastructure, Domain imports both Infrastructure and Presentation, Infrastructure imports Presentation, and Presentation imports Infrastructure. These cross-cuttings break encapsulation, create tight coupling, and prevent independent testing or technology substitution, resulting in a 60% health score.",
  "rationales": [
    {
      "violation_id": "main->presentation.api",
      "why_it_matters": "Application-layer code must not import Presentation-layer code; the dependency rule forbids outer layers from reaching inward. This creates tight coupling that prevents swapping UI frameworks or testing business logic in isolation.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Move application bootstrapping into a dedicated Composition Root or configuration module inside Presentation, or inject the 'app' interface as a parameter from Presentation into Application, reversing the dependency direction."
    },
    {
      "violation_id": "main->infrastructure.database",
      "why_it_matters": "Infrastructure is an outer implementation detail; Application-layer code must depend only on abstract ports, not concrete adapters. Direct imports tie core orchestration to a specific database implementation.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Define a 'DatabasePort' interface in Application, implement 'DatabasePort' in infrastructure.database, and inject the interface into main. Replace the direct 'init_db' import with dependency injection."
    },
    {
      "violation_id": "domain.fraud_checker->infrastructure.database",
      "why_it_matters": "Domain must remain free of infrastructure concerns; importing DatabaseConnection contaminates the pure business model with I/O dependencies and prevents testing without real database connections.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Create a 'FraudRepository' port (interface) in Domain, implement it in infrastructure.database, and inject the concrete repository into fraud_checker via constructor injection at runtime configuration."
    },
    {
      "violation_id": "domain.payment_rule->presentation.controllers",
      "why_it_matters": "Domain core logic must not know about UI formatting; importing ResponseFormatter violates the inward-only dependency rule and tightly couples business rules to a specific presentation format.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Define a 'PaymentResponse' port or DTO in Application, return plain domain objects from payment_rule, and let presentation.controllers map domain results to UI responses externally."
    },
    {
      "violation_id": "infrastructure.audit_logger->presentation.auth_middleware",
      "why_it_matters": "Infrastructure adapters should be agnostic of HTTP/web concerns; importing auth middleware couples logging to web middleware and prevents reuse in non-web contexts.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Define an 'AuditContext' port in Application, pass user context as method parameters from the Application layer, and have audit_logger consume plain context data instead of importing auth middleware."
    },
    {
      "violation_id": "presentation.order_routes->infrastructure.database",
      "why_it_matters": "Presentation must delegate persistence to Application Use-Cases; direct database imports bypass business rules, make testing mock-difficult, and bind web routes to a specific database driver.",
      "prescribed_fix": "Create an 'OrderService' use-case in Application, inject infrastructure.database as OrderRepository implementation, and have order_routes invoke OrderService instead of DatabaseConnection directly."
    }
  ],
  "roadmap": [
    "High priority: Fix main->presentation.api and main->infrastructure.database by introducing dependency injection or composition root patterns.",
    "High priority: Refactor domain.fraud_checker->infrastructure.database through a repository port/interface defined in Domain.",
    "High priority: Decouple domain.payment_rule->presentation.controllers by removing ResponseFormatter import and returning plain domain data.",
    "Medium priority: Separate infrastructure.audit_logger->presentation.auth_middleware by passing auth context as method parameters.",
    "Medium priority: Route presentation.order_routes->infrastructure.database through an Application-level OrderService use-case."
  ]
}

